Code is the better fix: it keeps the policy, privacy.md and architecture.md:137 true.

1. In apart's order c (build.rs:2985-2993), for each j, first try the j boxes the purpose would rather take: sort by `(!joins_base, purpose.rank, Reverse(lovelace))`. Then try the j largest where they differ, before moving to j + 1. Trying both before j + 1 answers R4-code's worry: two boxes are never merged where the larger alone pays. It also covers Mint, for a pool's start that reaches order c.

